== Data Structure Overview ==
'''Scribunto''' module (data base) for storing and configuring all possible entries (objects) for:
* [[Template:Obj]] (combines color & icon)
* [[Template:Color]] (color/classes related, text & link parameters)
* [[Template:I]] (icon parameter)
Object's existence is required within this module (for organization and other purposes) for it to work with the templates above<br>
To add color stylings, visit [[Template:Color/styles.css]]<br>
To add an entry to the data base, enter editing mode and add the following entry to appropriate location within the table (look for comments, they start with <code>--</code>):
<syntaxhighlight lang=lua>
["<Entry (object name)>"] = {
	"<Parameter (key)>" = "<Value>",
	...
},
</syntaxhighlight>
<Parameter> can be some or all of the following lines:<br>
<small>(ONLY PUT A VALUE IN IF IT'S REQUIRED FOR THE OBJECT)</small>
* <code>icon = <string>/false</code>
** Replaces the default '<object name>_Icon.png' file to the desired media
** '''false''' disables icon completely
* <code>link = <string>/false</code>
** Replaces the default object hyperlink (which is the object name itself) with <string>
** '''false''' removes hyperlink completely
* <code>plural = <string></code>
** provides plural form for the object template.
* <code>text = <string></code>
** Replaces object's name with a custom provided text by default
*** Can be used for objects with identical names or objects with unique symbols that can't be typed from standard US keyboard or any similar cases (e.g., Singularity (Layer) -> Singularity, Jalabono -> Jalaboño)
* <code>extraClass = <string></code>
** If color requires additional css classes, put any classes in a row separated by space
* <code>color = <string>/false</code>
** Applies (reuses) color of the specified object to that entry
*** Inherits "extraClass" and CSS variables
** '''false''' prevents any color classes from getting added